---
/**
 * Replaces Starlight's ThemeProvider, which reads `localStorage` and
 * `prefers-color-scheme` and can land the document in light mode.
 *
 * This site is dark only — it wears the catlog web app's dark palette, and the
 * app is the product it is documenting. So the document is stamped `dark`
 * unconditionally and there is nothing to read a preference from: the paired
 * `ThemeSelect.astro` override renders no toggle.
 *
 * The stamp matters even though `src/styles/custom.css` already forces the dark
 * values: several built-in components branch on the attribute itself rather
 * than on a colour (`<Badge>` swaps its variant backgrounds under
 * `[data-theme='light']:root`), so the attribute has to agree with the palette.
 */
---

{/* Inlined, not bundled, so the attribute is set before first paint. Starlight
    also renders dark by default when no attribute is present, so there is no
    light frame to flash even in the instant before this runs. */}
<script is:inline>
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
  // The stock ThemeSelect is gone, but leave the global callable in case any
  // other Starlight script reaches for it.
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = { updatePickers() {} };
</script>
